    {
      "id": "KtleCWdZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 820,
      "y": 1010,
      "width": 522,
      "height": 475,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0023",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1846411267,
      "version": 575,
      "versionNonce": 1846413062,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795070903234,
      "created": 1794322897544,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Transfer - one ACID transaction\n1. Verify auth; derive sender from caller ownership.\n   Validate MYR currency + positive integer amount.\n2. BEGIN; claim UNIQUE(caller, operation, key),\n   with a fingerprint of the transfer payload.\n3. Lock BOTH wallet rows, ascending wallet_id.\n   Recheck ownership + currency + available funds.\n4. Debit sender + credit recipient; insert transfer\n   and the immutable balanced ledger pair.\n5. Save idempotency result in this SAME transaction.\n6. COMMIT with required synchronous durability;\n   return success only after commit acknowledgement.\n\nPessimistic row locks serialize conflicting transfers.\n-> Check destination BIGINT overflow too\n-> Bound lock waits + transaction timeouts\n-> Roll back on failure; retry transient errors with\n   the same key, capped backoff + jitter\n-> No network calls while holding DB row locks",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Transfer - one ACID transaction\n1. Verify auth; derive sender from caller ownership.\n   Validate MYR currency + positive integer amount.\n2. BEGIN; claim UNIQUE(caller, operation, key),\n   with a fingerprint of the transfer payload.\n3. Lock BOTH wallet rows, ascending wallet_id.\n   Recheck ownership + currency + available funds.\n4. Debit sender + credit recipient; insert transfer\n   and the immutable balanced ledger pair.\n5. Save idempotency result in this SAME transaction.\n6. COMMIT with required synchronous durability;\n   return success only after commit acknowledgement.\n\nPessimistic row locks serialize conflicting transfers.\n-> Check destination BIGINT overflow too\n-> Bound lock waits + transaction timeouts\n-> Roll back on failure; retry transient errors with\n   the same key, capped backoff + jitter\n-> No network calls while holding DB row locks",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "rawText": "Transfer - one ACID transaction\n1. Verify auth; derive sender from caller ownership.\n   Validate MYR currency + positive integer amount.\n2. BEGIN; claim UNIQUE(caller, operation, key),\n   with a fingerprint of the transfer payload.\n3. Lock BOTH wallet rows, ascending wallet_id.\n   Recheck ownership + currency + available funds.\n4. Debit sender + credit recipient; insert transfer\n   and the immutable balanced ledger pair.\n5. Save idempotency result in this SAME transaction.\n6. COMMIT with required synchronous durability;\n   return success only after commit acknowledgement.\n\nPessimistic row locks serialize conflicting transfers.\n-> Check destination BIGINT overflow too\n-> Bound lock waits + transaction timeouts\n-> Roll back on failure; retry transient errors with\n   the same key, capped backoff + jitter\n-> No network calls while holding DB row locks"
    },
    {
      "id": "o1Rv1nYu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1680,
      "y": 1010,
      "width": 566,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0024",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 933076013,
      "version": 848,
      "versionNonce": 933077808,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795070903234,
      "created": 1794323666879,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Idempotency + crash recovery\nKey scoped to caller + operation; payload fingerprint\n-> Same key + payload: return saved result\n-> Same key + different payload: reject\n-> Concurrent duplicate: unique constraint arbitrates;\n   wait for original outcome, then replay/check payload\n\nCrash before commit?\n-> No committed transfer; retry with the same key\nCrash after commit, but response lost?\n-> Retry reads the result committed with the transfer\n\nKeep keys/results for the full supported retry window.\nAn expired or new key is not an unlimited retry guarantee.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Idempotency + crash recovery\nKey scoped to caller + operation; payload fingerprint\n-> Same key + payload: return saved result\n-> Same key + different payload: reject\n-> Concurrent duplicate: unique constraint arbitrates;\n   wait for original outcome, then replay/check payload\n\nCrash before commit?\n-> No committed transfer; retry with the same key\nCrash after commit, but response lost?\n-> Retry reads the result committed with the transfer\n\nKeep keys/results for the full supported retry window.\nAn expired or new key is not an unlimited retry guarantee.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "rawText": "Idempotency + crash recovery\nKey scoped to caller + operation; payload fingerprint\n-> Same key + payload: return saved result\n-> Same key + different payload: reject\n-> Concurrent duplicate: unique constraint arbitrates;\n   wait for original outcome, then replay/check payload\n\nCrash before commit?\n-> No committed transfer; retry with the same key\nCrash after commit, but response lost?\n-> Retry reads the result committed with the transfer\n\nKeep keys/results for the full supported retry window.\nAn expired or new key is not an unlimited retry guarantee."
    },
