      "rawText": "Optional history replica"
    },
    {
      "id": "8KT8M6Bo",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 90,
      "width": 568,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0051",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 437857187,
      "version": 406,
      "versionNonce": 437858982,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795070903234,
      "created": 1794326457866,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Security + reconciliation\nBackend verifies token with trusted keys + allowed\nsignature algorithm; check expiry, issuer, audience,\nrequired claims and revocation policy.\n-> Never trust a caller-supplied sender owner_id\n-> Authorize wallet access on every request\n\nPrevent incorrect postings in the write transaction.\nReconciliation is an additional detection control:\n-> Total debits = credits, per transfer + currency\n-> Compare wallet balances with immutable ledger totals\n-> Alert and investigate discrepancies\n-> Corrections use compensating entries; never edit ledger\n-> Avoid logging tokens or sensitive payment data",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Security + reconciliation\nBackend verifies token with trusted keys + allowed\nsignature algorithm; check expiry, issuer, audience,\nrequired claims and revocation policy.\n-> Never trust a caller-supplied sender owner_id\n-> Authorize wallet access on every request\n\nPrevent incorrect postings in the write transaction.\nReconciliation is an additional detection control:\n-> Total debits = credits, per transfer + currency\n-> Compare wallet balances with immutable ledger totals\n-> Alert and investigate discrepancies\n-> Corrections use compensating entries; never edit ledger\n-> Avoid logging tokens or sensitive payment data",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "rawText": "Security + reconciliation\nBackend verifies token with trusted keys + allowed\nsignature algorithm; check expiry, issuer, audience,\nrequired claims and revocation policy.\n-> Never trust a caller-supplied sender owner_id\n-> Authorize wallet access on every request\n\nPrevent incorrect postings in the write transaction.\nReconciliation is an additional detection control:\n-> Total debits = credits, per transfer + currency\n-> Compare wallet balances with immutable ledger totals\n-> Alert and investigate discrepancies\n-> Corrections use compensating entries; never edit ledger\n-> Avoid logging tokens or sensitive payment data"
    },
    {
      "id": "KDViOgC7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 560,
      "width": 565,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0052",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 352077453,
      "version": 1578,
      "versionNonce": 352079248,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795070903234,
      "created": 1794326809564,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Hot wallet + overload protection\nA busy merchant serializes on the destination row.\nUser rate limits alone do not protect that row.\n\nBefore taking DB connections:\n-> Per-wallet in-flight limits for BOTH wallets\n-> Global in-flight cap across service instances\n-> Coordinate admission across instances if needed\n-> Bound queue length + waits; time out quickly\n-> Redis is optional for shared admission / rate limits\n\nKeep DB locks short + connection pool bounded.\nReturn 429 + Retry-After when admission is full.\n-> Capped exponential backoff + random jitter\n-> Reuse original idempotency key on every retry\n-> Prevent retries from multiplying the overload\n\nProtect destination contention, not just sender fairness.\nMore service instances do not raise DB write capacity.\nA queue does not increase sustained DB throughput.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Hot wallet + overload protection\nA busy merchant serializes on the destination row.\nUser rate limits alone do not protect that row.\n\nBefore taking DB connections:\n-> Per-wallet in-flight limits for BOTH wallets\n-> Global in-flight cap across service instances\n-> Coordinate admission across instances if needed\n-> Bound queue length + waits; time out quickly\n-> Redis is optional for shared admission / rate limits\n\nKeep DB locks short + connection pool bounded.\nReturn 429 + Retry-After when admission is full.\n-> Capped exponential backoff + random jitter\n-> Reuse original idempotency key on every retry\n-> Prevent retries from multiplying the overload\n\nProtect destination contention, not just sender fairness.\nMore service instances do not raise DB write capacity.\nA queue does not increase sustained DB throughput.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "rawText": "Hot wallet + overload protection\nA busy merchant serializes on the destination row.\nUser rate limits alone do not protect that row.\n\nBefore taking DB connections:\n-> Per-wallet in-flight limits for BOTH wallets\n-> Global in-flight cap across service instances\n-> Coordinate admission across instances if needed\n-> Bound queue length + waits; time out quickly\n-> Redis is optional for shared admission / rate limits\n\nKeep DB locks short + connection pool bounded.\nReturn 429 + Retry-After when admission is full.\n-> Capped exponential backoff + random jitter\n-> Reuse original idempotency key on every retry\n-> Prevent retries from multiplying the overload\n\nProtect destination contention, not just sender fairness.\nMore service instances do not raise DB write capacity.\nA queue does not increase sustained DB throughput."
    },
