    {
      "id": "by3gOpXv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2520,
      "y": 1240,
      "width": 559,
      "height": 400,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0056",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 712319981,
      "version": 96,
      "versionNonce": 712321776,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795070903234,
      "created": 1794327129400,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Trade offs - measure before adding complexity\nStart with one modular service + one primary database.\nMultiple instances provide service capacity / availability.\n\nDefer microservices, Kafka, sharding, and cross-DB\ntransactions until measurements justify their cost.\n-> No Redis distributed lock for transfer atomicity\n-> No two-phase commit in this single-DB baseline\n\nLoad test realistic balances + history + concurrent\ntransfers at the target peak, with hot merchant skew.\n-> Measure p95 latency, lock waits, pool saturation,\n   database CPU / I/O, storage and replication lag\n-> Tune queries + indexes + hardware first\n-> Shard only after a measured limit; cross-shard money\n   then needs a separately designed consistency protocol",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Trade offs - measure before adding complexity\nStart with one modular service + one primary database.\nMultiple instances provide service capacity / availability.\n\nDefer microservices, Kafka, sharding, and cross-DB\ntransactions until measurements justify their cost.\n-> No Redis distributed lock for transfer atomicity\n-> No two-phase commit in this single-DB baseline\n\nLoad test realistic balances + history + concurrent\ntransfers at the target peak, with hot merchant skew.\n-> Measure p95 latency, lock waits, pool saturation,\n   database CPU / I/O, storage and replication lag\n-> Tune queries + indexes + hardware first\n-> Shard only after a measured limit; cross-shard money\n   then needs a separately designed consistency protocol",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "rawText": "Trade offs - measure before adding complexity\nStart with one modular service + one primary database.\nMultiple instances provide service capacity / availability.\n\nDefer microservices, Kafka, sharding, and cross-DB\ntransactions until measurements justify their cost.\n-> No Redis distributed lock for transfer atomicity\n-> No two-phase commit in this single-DB baseline\n\nLoad test realistic balances + history + concurrent\ntransfers at the target peak, with hot merchant skew.\n-> Measure p95 latency, lock waits, pool saturation,\n   database CPU / I/O, storage and replication lag\n-> Tune queries + indexes + hardware first\n-> Shard only after a measured limit; cross-shard money\n   then needs a separately designed consistency protocol"
    },
